meta {
  name: Logout
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/auth/logout
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  ~Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "refresh_token": "{{refresh_token}}",
    "all": false
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 200) {
    bru.setEnvVar("access_token", "");
    bru.setEnvVar("refresh_token", "");
  }
}

docs {
  # POST /auth/logout
  
  Invalidate refresh token(s). Optionally revoke all sessions for the user.
  
  ## HTTP Method & Route
  - **Method:** `POST`
  - **Route:** `/wp-json/tutor/v1/auth/logout`
  
  ## Authentication
  - **Type:** Public for single-token logout; Bearer recommended when `all: true`
  
  ## Request Body
  
  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
  | `refresh_token` | `string` | No* | Specific refresh token to revoke (hash removed from that user’s stored list). |
  | `all` | `boolean` | No | When `true`, bump `token_version` and delete all refresh tokens for the user. Resolves the user from Bearer access token, or from a valid `refresh_token` if Bearer is absent. |
  
  \* Provide `refresh_token` and/or set `all: true` with a Bearer token (or a valid `refresh_token` to identify the user). Omitting both still returns success but revokes nothing.
  
  ## Responses
  
  ### 200 OK (Success)
  ```json
  {
    "code": "tutor_auth_logout",
    "message": "Logged out successfully.",
    "data": {
      "success": true
    }
  }
  ```
}
